  "notes": "{済|す}ませる means to finish, complete, or settle something. It emphasizes getting something done or out of the way.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {済|す}む (intransitive - to be finished/done)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xを{済|す}ませる: to finish X\n- Xで{済|す}ませる: to settle with X, to manage with just X\n- {先|さき}に{済|す}ませる: to get done first\n- {早|はや}く{済|す}ませる: to finish quickly\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {仕事|しごと}を{済|す}ませる: to finish work\n- {食事|しょくじ}を{済|す}ませる: to finish a meal\n- {用事|ようじ}を{済|す}ませる: to finish errands\n- {手続|てつづ}きを{済|す}ませる: to complete procedures\n\nSIMILAR VERBS:\n- {終|お}える: to finish, complete (neutral)\n- {済|す}ませる: to get done, settle (emphasis on disposing of)\n- {片付|かたづ}ける: to tidy up, finish off",
